      "description": "Current topics illustrating important research field in materials science will be discussed. Topics covered will include: energy materials, biomaterials, and computational material science. The course provides an introduction to the background concept, physical principles and applications of the relevant material systems.",
      "enrollment_requirement": "For students in MSc Physics, MPhil-PhD Materials Sci & Erg or MPhil-PhD Physics",
      "course_attributes": "",
      "academic_career": "Postgraduate - Research",
      "grading_basis": "Graded",
      "component": "Lecture",
      "campus": "Main Campus",
      "academic_group": "Div of Material Science & Erg",
      "academic_org": "Div of Material Science & Erg",
      "learning_outcomes": "Students at the end of the course are expected to have gained an appreciation of the fundamental concepts as well as the state of art methodologies in frontiers of materials research. They are expected to have gained the ability to operationalize these concepts in precise frameworks, and to have the ability to pursue these topics in further depth beyond this course. Some of the material will have to be learnt by the student on their own, and through this activity students will develop the capability and habit of self-directed learning.",
      "assessment_types": {
        "Presentation": "52",
        "Test or quiz": "48"
      }
    },
